{
  "$schema": "../schemas/looks.schema.json",
  "$comment": "Hero looks (docs/hero-looks.md §3.1, §6, §7): the one catalog of coats, specials, nameplate frames and titles a hero may choose. Mirrors LookCatalog in packages/shared/src/types/look.ts. Starter looks are free for every hero and never stored; every other look is held through a receipt on her own look (LookUnlock). Earned ones are given by a receipt (#669, packages/shared/src/look-unlocks.ts): a found look by a chapter's findLook effect (content/README.md, Look finds), a milestone (tier, class rank, finished campaign, camp friend, first friend, grand camp) when it lands and on read. Coats are colours for one part of one species: every species has a main part (look.coat) and an accent part (look.accent), named in assets/manifest.json -> coatMasks.regions (a unicorn's coat and mane, a Bigfoot's fur and skin), and the book shows one shelf per part under its name. About six starters per part per species, natural for it; each set is checked against its siblings under colour-blind vision, and the main part's against every backdrop, by packages/client/src/world/coat-palette.test.ts. Her two colours are never checked against each other: the pair is hers. Specials (owner, 2026-11-07) are not colours: they apply across her whole figure, every species alike, and are earned only. sparkle: twinkling sparkles over her. gilded: the whole figure swapped toward its color, keeping its lightness steps, her colours ignored. A frame's painting is UI art (#665) at assets/<art>; until assets/manifest.json -> nameplateFrames.ids lists it as delivered, the plain plate (today's look) is drawn instead and nothing is requested. Titles are kept short: the longest one is what the nameplate collision tests are run with.",
